 "notes": "Habili Neilson (Sha'ab el Nabaa, Nelson Reef): a submerged reef about 50 m long with its top at 3-5 m, a deeper plateau at each end (10-15 m east, 17-20 m west), a wall to about 21 m, sand at 23-25 m and pinnacles mainly on the north side. Oriented east-west and centred on the small reef OpenStreetMap shows at the site position. Which plateau lies at which end, the pinnacle positions and the drift line are approximate.",
